course: dictionary
lesson: 7788
title: A word from a dance floor
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: A quadrille is an old word you may not know, so read the words around it for clues. «Then the two creatures excitedly explain the Lobster Quadrille, a seaside dance: two lines of seals, turtles and salmon, each with a lobster for a partner». Lines, partners and dance are clues: a quadrille must be a kind of dance.
explain: «A quadrille is an old-fashioned dance for couples, done in steps called «figures»». Here the context tells you more: the dance has parts, and each part is a figure. Try your meaning in the sentence: "A dance done in steps called figures" makes sense, so your meaning is probably right.
explain: The start of the word gives a clue too. Quad- comes from Latin and French words for four, just like quadrilateral, a shape with four sides. A quadrille was danced by four couples standing in a square, so the name fits the shape of the dance.
fact: A quadrille is an old dance for four couples standing in a square.
fact: The dance was done in several parts, and it was popular in the 1800s.
fact: Quadrille can also mean the music for this dance, or an old card game for four players.
fact: In «Alice in Wonderland», the Mock Turtle and the Gryphon dance the Lobster Quadrille for Alice.
fact: Quad- means four, as in quadrilateral.
exercise: «Then the two creatures excitedly explain the Lobster Quadrille, a seaside dance». What kind of thing is a quadrille? | A sea creature | A poem about a lobster | *A dance | A card game for two
exercise: «A quadrille is an old-fashioned dance for couples, done in steps called figures». What are the steps of the dance called? | Lines | *Figures | Seals | Partners
exercise: The root quad- means four. Which word shares this Latin and French root? | *Quadrilateral | Triangle | Decade | Octopus
test: In which century was the quadrille popular? | The 1500s | The 1900s | *The 1800s | The 1200s
test: «Shall we try another figure of the Lobster Quadrille?» What does figure mean here? | *One of the steps or parts of the dance | A drawing of a person | A type of seal | A number
exam: Based on the context, which best describes a quadrille? | A slow song sung at a funeral | A card game for four players only | A seaside creature with claws | *An old dance for four couples, done in several parts
